Subject: register VM folds a global `undefined` read to a constant

What this does:
  Box2D reads the global `undefined` constantly (the default-argument guards and
  the compare-and-branches that 0145 addressed all start from one). The lowered
  form is `ROP_get_global`, which probes the runtime's global-name cell and checks
  its generation before it can answer, on every execution -- for an atom whose
  answer cannot change.

  `undefined` is not writable and not configurable (ES §19.1.4), every realm's
  `undefined` is the same immediate `JS_MKVAL(JS_TAG_UNDEFINED, 0)`, and the
  global read path in the register backend is only reached after scope
  resolution has already failed. So a `var`, `let` or `undefined` binding in this
  function or any of its parents would have resolved to a register/local instead
  of falling through to the global. `with` emits its own `OP_with_get_var` checks
  ahead of the fallback. The one construct that could install a binding the
  static scope chain does not show is a direct `eval`, and `has_eval_call` is
  exactly that predicate, so the fold is skipped when it is set anywhere in the
  `fd->parent` chain.

      case OP_get_var:
          if (get_u32(bc + pos + 1) == JS_ATOM_undefined) {
              const JSFunctionDef *q_;
              int ev = 0;
              for (q_ = fd; q_; q_ = q_->parent)
                  if (q_->has_eval_call)
                      ev = 1;
              if (!ev) {
                  ADD(ROP_load_undefined, dst);
                  return 0;
              }
          }
          ADD(ROP_get_global, dst, ...);

  `OP_get_var_undef` (the form whose answer may be `undefined` when the binding
  is missing) is deliberately left alone: its two results are not the same.
  Folding at the stack-bytecode level instead -- letting the peephole recognise
  the `undefined` literal and emit `OP_is_undefined` -- measured *worse* (+0.09 G
  instructions), because it disturbs the surrounding lowering, so the fold stays
  in `regvm_lower_insn`.

  On `check.js` the ROP counts move `get_global` 13.47 M -> 4.60 M and
  `load_undefined` 6.94 M -> 15.81 M.

  Measured (`fixed.js`, 32 iterations, i7-8700), on top of 0146: 23,600,642,543
  -> 23,449,645,130 instructions (**-0.151 G, -0.64 %**), against the plan's
  0.145 G expected. Gate run: 23,447,318,225 / 11,288,401,824 (cycles flat
  within noise). Checksum `546.1008391043414` exact; diff-suite `pass=398
  fail=0 skip=0` mono and threaded; leak assertion clean; peak RSS 13228 KB.

No opcode, operand encoding or serialized register-format change.
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -56239,6 +56239,28 @@
 
     /* globals */
     case OP_get_var:
+        /*
+         * `undefined` is a non-writable, non-configurable global (ES §19.1.4)
+         * and every realm's `undefined` is the same immediate, so a read of it
+         * is a constant -- unless a direct `eval` in this function or one of
+         * its parents could have introduced a lexical `undefined` binding. The
+         * global read is only reached after scope resolution fails, so a
+         * `var`/`let`/`undefined` binding anywhere would have resolved there;
+         * `with` emits its own `OP_with_get_var` ahead of the fallback, so it is
+         * covered too. Folding to `ROP_load_undefined` removes a global-cell
+         * probe and its generation check from a very common read.
+         */
+        if (get_u32(bc + pos + 1) == JS_ATOM_undefined) {
+            const JSFunctionDef *q_;
+            int ev = 0;
+            for (q_ = fd; q_; q_ = q_->parent)
+                if (q_->has_eval_call)
+                    ev = 1;
+            if (!ev) {
+                ADD(ROP_load_undefined, dst);
+                return 0;
+            }
+        }
         ADD(ROP_get_global, dst, (int32_t)get_u32(bc + pos + 1), 1); return 0;
     case OP_get_var_undef:
         ADD(ROP_get_global, dst, (int32_t)get_u32(bc + pos + 1), 0); return 0;
